        "raw": "<p>So I had a fun scenario recently. Since it was on the video game, I did not break the rules or read the cards wrong. But I would like to get the experts opinions on this.</p><p>The Adventure of Prime Warden Captain&#39;s Cosmic and his ability to play and destroy all that he holds (like cards) dear.</p><p>Note that Infinitor is the villain</p><p>Prime Wardens Captain Cosmic has the following</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3 Cards in Hand, &quot;Construct Cataclysm&quot;, &quot;Potent Disruption&quot;, and &quot;Conservation of Energy&quot;</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 6 Constructs in play</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Activated his base Power &quot;Absorption&quot;</p><p>What happened.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A Construct gets destroyed from an outside source (let&#39;s say the environment). This activates CC&#39;s power.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I shuffled his construct back in deck and played &quot;Conservation of Energy, destroying all my constructs to draw more cards.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The first of the 5 gets destroyed, I shuffle and play &quot;Construct Cataclysm&quot;.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; (This is where things get complicated)</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I played as many Constructs as I could until I had no more in hand</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I played &quot;Potent Disruption&quot; on the final one to give that extra boost.</p><p>Let&#39;s say I was only able to draw 3 constructs from Absorption.</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; What&#39;s the most damage I could do? (Pending that I only drew 3 construct cards)</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; What would be the best order to play the cards?</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; With the combination of Absorption and playing multiple &quot;Conservation of Energy&quot;, I could potentially go for as long as I can play Constructs. But this <strong>WON&#39;T </strong>result in infinite damage. Is this statement correct?</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Can I benefit the outcomes of &quot;Construct Cataclysm&quot;, &quot;Potent Disruption&quot;, and &quot;Conservation of Energy&quot; from a single construct? (Fixed Point is not in play, even if it was, I don&#39;t know what would happen)</p><p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; What would happen if &quot;Fixed Point&quot; was in play? Would no damage be dealt, would CC not draw/play any cards?</p><p>I played this on the videogame (on my phone), and so I don&#39;t recall exactly what the steps I took.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
